its with one  another came up and received his  judgement then he returned into the  house and received ambassador's of  barbarous people's we're ovate it to a  banquet with a teller at three o'clock  when the hour arrived we went to the  palace along with the embassy from the  Western Roman's and stood on the  threshold of the hall in the presence of  Attila  [Music]  the cupbearers gave us a cuff according  to the national custom that we might  pray before we sat down having tasted  the cup we proceeded to take our seats  all the chairs being arranged along the  wall of the room on either side attila  sat in the middle on a couch a second  couch was set behind him and from its  steps led up to his bed which was  covered with the linen sheets and  wrought coverlets  for ornament such as Greeks and Romans  used to deck bridal beds the places on  the right of Attila were held chief in  honor those on the left where we sat  were only second first the king and his  guests pledged one another with the wine  when this ceremony was over the cup  bearers retired and tables large enough  for three or four even more to sit at  were placed next to the table of a  tiller so that each could take of the  food on the dishes without leaving his  seat the attendant of a tiller first  entered with a dish full of meat and  behind him came the other attendants  with bread and viens which they lay on  the tables a luxurious meal served on  silver plate had been made ready for us  and the barbarian guests but Attila  ain't nothing but meat on a wooden  trencher in everything else too he  showed himself temperate his cup was of  wood while to the guests were given  goblets of gold and silver his dress too  was quite simple affecting only to be  clean the sword he carried at his side  the latch 'it's of his civilian shoes  the bridle of his horse were not adorned  like those of the other Citians with  gold or gems or anything costly when the  viens of the first course had been  consumed we all stood up did not resumed  our seats until each one in the order  before observed drank to the health of  Attila in the goblet of wine presented  to him we then sat down  and the second dish was placed on each  table with eatables of another kind  after this course the same ceremony was  observed as after the first when evening  fell torches were lit and two barbarians  coming forward in front of Attila sang  songs they had composed celebrating his  victories and diesel valor in war  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

